# Written in place by `just activate`. Do not fill these by hand: the chat uid
# and token are minted together by the activation exchange, and a hand-typed
# pair that does not match will authenticate as nothing.
#
# The token that lands here is ROWAN's Plow credential, not the operator's.
# POST /v1/auth/activate takes no credential at all — the binding is whichever
# phone texts the code back — so this is his account, and the plow-connectors
# skill reusing this same token is what makes it his mail, his calendar and his
# Slack rather than anyone else's.
#
# Activation also writes PLOW_CHAT_BASE_URL and PLOW_CHAT_HOME_CHANNEL. They are
# absent here because nothing chooses them: the script derives both.
PLOW_CHAT_CHAT_UID=
PLOW_CHAT_TOKEN=
